<title>CHILE: Finnish president arrives in Chile for trade talks.</title>
<headline>Finnish president arrives in Chile for trade talks.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish President Martti Ahtisaari arrived in Chile on Wednesday for a visit aimed at strengthening growing trade and investment ties, including in copper mining in which Finland is a major investor in Chile.</p>
<p>Ahtissari will meet Chilean business leaders and discuss investments in industries including copper, paper and forestry and telecommunications, said Chilean officials.</p>
<p>Finland is already the fourth largest European investor in Chile. Helsinki-based mining company Outokumpu is co-owner of the large Zaldivar copper mine in northern Chile and announced plans this week to build an $800 million copper refinery with Chilean power company Endesa.</p>
</text>
